cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "CliffordClock: optical-atomic-clock DC-Stark and
  second-order Doppler shift calculations via Spacetime Algebra Cl(1,3)
  rotor dynamics"
abstract: >-
  CliffordClock is an open-source Python/JAX library that computes
  optical-atomic-clock fractional frequency shifts (target regime: 1e-18
  level) caused by stray static (DC) electric fields and by the atom's
  own motion. It evaluates the second-order (quadratic) DC-Stark shift
  for J=0->J=0 lattice clocks and the second-order (kinematic) Doppler
  shift, using a proper-time/phase-accumulation model built on a
  Spacetime Algebra Cl(1,3) rotor formalism. See docs/validation.md in
  the repository for the current validation status.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rudolph"
    given-names: "Michael"
